{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev","id":349040,"title":"The Scintillating Flame \u2013 Qashmallim(Open Dev)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-24T07:37:06-08:00","id":349040,"title":"The Scintillating Flame \u2013 Qashmallim(Open Dev)","content":"So, new update. Here we go: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-scintillating-flame-qashmallim-promethean-the-created/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/11/OPP-Metal.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-scintillating-flame-qashmallim-promethean-the-created/\" target=\"_blank\"> The Scintillating Flame &ndash; Qashmallim [Promethean: The Created] &ndash; Onyx Path Publishing </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-scintillating-flame-qashmallim-promethean-the-created/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://theonyxpath.com/the-scintillating-flame-qashmallim-promethean-the-created/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Find the fact that the Flux creature is actually doing a good deed interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T14:22:57-08:00","id":349287,"title":"","content":"That's awesome. I really like anything that merges the supernatural metaphysics with the everyday world; it makes the setting feel more organic. I think Demon suffers a little by lacking that element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T17:49:09-08:00","id":349428,"title":"","content":"I mentioned this in the post's comments, buuuuuuuuut...<br /> <br /> No mention of the ever-mysterious third choir. I wonder if they're still a thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T18:10:48-08:00","id":349435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=349428#post349428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mentioned this in the post's comments, buuuuuuuuut...<br /> <br /> No mention of the ever-mysterious third choir. I wonder if they're still a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to have to elaborate, because the nearest thing I can think of is the arch-qashmallim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T22:03:25-08:00","id":349565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=349435#post349435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're going to have to elaborate, because the nearest thing I can think of is the arch-qashmallim.</div> </div> </div> </div>In addition to the Elpidos and the Lillithim, I had recalled rumors of a third Choir. On further reading it turns out I was remembering there are rumors of the third Order of Arch-quashmallim. I've kind of run with the idea of a third Choir in my headcanon since then, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T00:42:51-08:00","id":349687,"title":"","content":"Okay, unless the author was being poetic the Principle is the collective will of pyros itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T08:33:28-08:00","id":349859,"title":"","content":"I have a couple of questions.<br /> If I understood correctly we have four types of beings that <u><b><i>could</i></b> </u>be considered angels. The servants of the god-machine, the beings invoked form the astral plane from mages, the <i>qashmallim</i>from the pyros and the spirit entities associated to the virtues of humanity, am I correct?<br /> How do you integrate the <i>qashmallim</i>in your unified world of darkness universe if you have one? Are they the servants of the one and true creator? Is pyros the unrefined source of all other kinds of methapysical energy? Does the principle have a will of its own or it is just a force of the universe? Is the god machine and impostor, a pretender or a servant of the principle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T10:00:48-08:00","id":349928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=349687#post349687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, unless the author was being poetic the Principle is the collective will of pyros itself.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is my preferred version (I wrote the <i>qashmallim</i> section for Promethean second edition) - the Principle is the emergent collective will of Pyros.<br /> <br /> Note that that doesn't mean it isn't also &quot;God.&quot;<br /> <br /> But, then, I always push the &quot;the God-Machine isn't a seperate entity, it's the sum total of all Infrastructure&quot; thing as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In addition to the Elpidos and the Lillithim, I had recalled rumors of a third Choir. </div> </div> </div>One of the things Wood Ingham did in his <i>qashmallim</i> section of Pandora's Book, which I read about twenty times before writing them up for 2E, was point out that there's really no such thing as &quot;Elpidos&quot; or &quot;Lilithim&quot;. Or for that matter Elpis or Flux - it's all just Pyros. The choirs and orders were made up by alchemists and Prometheans to try to classify what they were seeing - no <i>qashmal</i> ever calls itself &quot;a greater Lilithim&quot; or whathaveyou. Or, for that matter, no <i>qashmal</i> ever calls itself a &quot;<i>qashmal</i>&quot; - if you ask one what it is, it'll just say &quot;A Messenger&quot; or &quot;an Agent.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T14:19:55-08:00","id":350056,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the Principle being God and the God-Machine a Usurper.<br /> By the way, in a unrelated note, what exactly the word qashmallim means? It is made up or does it have any real meaning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T14:38:42-08:00","id":350065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350056#post350056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea of the Principle being God and the God-Machine a Usurper.<br /> By the way, in a unrelated note, what exactly the word qashmallim means? It is made up or does it have any real meaning?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hashmal\" target=\"_blank\">*cough*</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T14:44:02-08:00","id":350068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350065#post350065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hashmal\" target=\"_blank\">*cough*</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T15:07:18-08:00","id":350074,"title":"","content":"I have an idea, what if the god machine was one of the first qashmallim created by the principle? during his service either something went horribly wrong and changed or he decided that he could do a better job and rebelled. what do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T15:13:05-08:00","id":350077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350074#post350074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea, what if the god machine was one of the first qashmallim created by the principle? during his service either something went horribly wrong and changed or he decided that he could do a better job and rebelled. what do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>What if the God-Machine was a creation of the Principle that was made to give the universe some Infrastructure and went rogue or was damaged?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T15:15:35-08:00","id":350079,"title":"","content":"Anyway back on the Qashmallin, it seens they are much more involved on the affairs of the Prometheans than they were in the 1ed. Wonder if they mess as much with Pandorans and Alchemists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T15:16:39-08:00","id":350080,"title":"","content":"I don't like it. It makes cosmic forces seem far too human. Further, how would you actually use this in a game? The GM could easily be a giant qashmallim, that's fine. But how would you distinguish between a qashmaillim doing it's intended job, and it rebelling?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T16:19:41-08:00","id":350120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350080#post350080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like it. It makes cosmic forces seem far too human. Further, how would you actually use this in a game? The GM could easily be a giant qashmallim, that's fine. But how would you distinguish between a qashmaillim doing it's intended job, and it rebelling?</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't, for me that is part of the horror, the gm is the only one who has all the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T21:54:15-08:00","id":350398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350120#post350120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't, for me that is part of the horror, the gm is the only one who has all the answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being that it's essentially a giant decentralized Unchained in terms of trustworthiness of answers, &quot;this thing that dispatches beings resembling angels is causally related to this other thing that dispatches beings resembling angels&quot; is in general kind of a tiresome theory to me, particularly when it stops at &quot;the thing with a stronger foothold on the world is a rip-off of the other thing that doesn't demonstrate much greater potency.&quot; Also, both the entities we're talking about are vast enough to apparently entertain directly contradictory trains of thought; you could definitely make more of the weird symmetry the Fire and the Machine exhibit than &quot;one made the other.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-26-2014, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-25T22:12:49-08:00","id":350405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350080#post350080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like it. It makes cosmic forces seem far too human.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love it for this exact reason.<br /> <br /> I don't care much for cosmic horror in and of itself- the idea that I should be cowed by an infinite and uncaring world has always struck hollow for me. So having cosmic forces demonstrate themselves as being prone to bouts of humanity not only makes them more erratic and fearful, it just avoids a trite trope altogether.<br /> <br /> Two of my favorite examples of this trend in nWoD are the Idigam and the Shan'iatu. These guys should be poster children for cosmic horror, but no, they get personal, and show all the signs of their circumstances in very human terms, and they are more frightening for their warped intimacy than their alien distance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T01:34:19-08:00","id":350524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350405#post350405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two of my favorite examples of this trend in nWoD are the Idigam and the Shan'iatu. These guys should be poster children for cosmic horror, but no, they get personal, and show all the signs of their circumstances in very human terms, and they are more frightening for their warped intimacy than their alien distance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arc, the temakh got weaker as they got more involved with humanity and Mummy's stance on power isn't exactly an isolated theme in the WoD, to say nothing of how &quot;the most powerful one of these things that we encountered was Rank 6&quot; is not equivalent to &quot;cosmic forces.&quot;<br /> <br /> If I want the broken architects of the universe and their peers to be humans-writ-large I can pop on over to Exalted, where that is a direct statement of developer intent. I come to nWoD for the wondrous and terrifying alien occult substrata of the world and its general incompatibility with a healthy human perspective.<br /> <br /> The Shan'iatu and the idigam are not <i>systems</i> lessened in perceived scale by being compared to discrete individual beings. That's like comparing a government official to <i>the continent of Australia.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T03:35:13-08:00","id":350555,"title":"","content":"It's not about cosmic horror it's about the sublime. The idea that humans are ultimately just part of a far larger universe, and it doesn't revolve around us. Think the Sun rather than Cthulhu. It's vast, powerful, and we all actually rely on it. However, it's just a star; it doesn't care about us.When it's sunny, it's not being nice to us, when it's winter it's not sulking.<br /> <br /> I think the horror in the setting comes precisely when you start adding in individuals with agendas. The sueprnal doesn't care about humans, the Exarchs do. The Temakh story is precisely about them bending these wondrous bit impersonal cosmic forces to ultimately petty and very human ends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T06:25:30-08:00","id":350603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350080#post350080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how would you distinguish between a qashmaillim doing it's intended job, and it rebelling?</div> </div> </div> </div>Qashamlim can't rebel, at least according to the first edition; they can't process any thought outside their Mission. Even if you could somehow bind one, telling it to violate its Mission wouldn't work, because it wouldn't understand what you were trying to get it to do.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T08:31:06-08:00","id":350668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350555#post350555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about cosmic horror it's about the sublime. The idea that humans are ultimately just part of a far larger universe, and it doesn't revolve around us. Think the Sun rather than Cthulhu. It's vast, powerful, and we all actually rely on it. However, it's just a star; it doesn't care about us.When it's sunny, it's not being nice to us, when it's winter it's not sulking.<br /> <br /> I think the horror in the setting comes precisely when you start adding in individuals with agendas. The sueprnal doesn't care about humans, the Exarchs do. The Temakh story is precisely about them bending these wondrous bit impersonal cosmic forces to ultimately petty and very human ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>...And?<br /> <br /> I haven't caught precisely what you're getting at, but I fail to see how that's lessened because Pyros is directly linked to human behaviors. Discovering that stuff is alive in some strange sense doesn't lessen the mystery, or the fear; to invoke a different media, it's like lyrium in Dragon Age; already the stuff was one of the most dangerous and intriguing materials in the setting, it both driving people batty and being the ultimate source of magic. In Inquisition, we incidentally discover that it's actually alive when we realize how the more dangerous red lyrium is formed-namely, that it's ghoul lyrium, and nonliving things can't become ghouls. This actually makes lyrium more mysterious, because apart from that, we know <i>nothing </i>about the stuff. We can assume the stuff grows given how aggressively red lyrium will infect and colonize everything if given half a chance, but apart from that? Nothing. Could be our equivalent to something Lovecraftian, could be something entirely incidental.<br /> <br /> Pyros is much the same way. It lives and thinks, but we humans are not privy to its mind or its functions. It could love us, because we feed it...but the existence of Extempores implies that it doesn't actually need us. It could also be that &quot;thinking&quot; isn't a great description of what it does, it just acts like a thinking thing because we don't understand its nature well enough (see; nature, every just so story, ever). It's just as likely that it's not so much humans it supports to much as sapience; again, sapience feeds it. To put it bluntly, nobody really knows, and ignorance is only bliss in that you can't see the thing about to kill you.<br /> <br /> (That, and given such a fundamentally humanistic game as Promethean, cosmicism seems rather counterproductive to all the other themes. There might be cosmic horror elements, but making that a focus seems...self-defeating).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T08:54:33-08:00","id":350684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350668#post350668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't caught precisely what you're getting at, but I fail to see how that's lessened because Pyros is directly linked to human behaviors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lel, I realize it's difficult to keep track of a conversation when one or more parties has neglected the Quote button, but Michael's &quot;I don't like it&quot; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350074#post350074\">is not directed at the blog entry</a>, as one would hope was evident from his <i>immediately expanding on that statement in terms of &quot;what is the utility of 'the God-Machine is a giant qashmallim'?&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T11:39:32-08:00","id":350809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350524#post350524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arc, the temakh got weaker as they got more involved with humanity and Mummy's stance on power isn't exactly an isolated theme in the WoD, to say nothing of how &quot;the most powerful one of these things that we encountered was Rank 6&quot; is not equivalent to &quot;cosmic forces.&quot;<br /> <br /> If I want the broken architects of the universe and their peers to be humans-writ-large I can pop on over to Exalted, where that is a direct statement of developer intent. I come to nWoD for the wondrous and terrifying alien occult substrata of the world and its general incompatibility with a healthy human perspective.<br /> <br /> The Shan'iatu and the idigam are not <i>systems</i> lessened in perceived scale by being compared to discrete individual beings. That's like comparing a government official to <i>the continent of Australia.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T12:40:17-08:00","id":350854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=349928#post349928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things Wood Ingham did in his <i>qashmallim</i> section of Pandora's Book, which I read about twenty times before writing them up for 2E, was point out that there's really no such thing as &quot;Elpidos&quot; or &quot;Lilithim&quot;. Or for that matter Elpis or Flux - it's all just Pyros. The choirs and orders were made up by alchemists and Prometheans to try to classify what they were seeing - no <i>qashmal</i> ever calls itself &quot;a greater Lilithim&quot; or whathaveyou. Or, for that matter, no <i>qashmal</i> ever calls itself a &quot;<i>qashmal</i>&quot; - if you ask one what it is, it'll just say &quot;A Messenger&quot; or &quot;an Agent.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like how this invites questions about the qashmallim's relationship with the God-Machine's angels and the Unchained.<br /> <br /> On a side note, why do the books always italicize qashmal and qashmllim? Is it because they're words from another language?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","user":"Metamurpho","date":". 12-26-2014, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T13:32:05-08:00","id":350875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350603#post350603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Qashamlim can't rebel</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm aware. It says so in this update. However, it was the basic notion behind Firanai's idea. Even then, there's always room for one exception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T14:01:11-08:00","id":350904,"title":"","content":"My suggestion was just that, a suggestion, I don't know all the rules or background of new world of darkness so assume that some times I make mistakes due to my ignorance. My suggestion was less about the nature of the pyros and the <i>Qashamlim </i> and more about an effort to connect the different universes together.<br /> I know that each line of the new world of darkness is made with the idea to be it's own universe separated from the other lines. I'm OK with it sine it gives you free reign to design your cosmos the way you like it.<br /> However my group, and specially me, we prefer the idea of a unified cosmos with all the lines together and related to each other. We have been discussing ideas on how to do this starting with having mage the awakening as the main line or cosmology and building from there.<br /> I already received some ideas for mage and demon in the discussion of exarchs vs god machine and reading this blog post I was wondering how demon, the god machine and Promethean could fit together. Then we can see how to fit it in mage. I would like to hear your suggestions and ideas while being as faithful to the rules and the setting as possible. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T14:03:56-08:00","id":350905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350684#post350684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lel, I realize it's difficult to keep track of a conversation when one or more parties has neglected the Quote button, but Michael's &amp;quot;I don't like it&amp;quot; <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350074#post350074&amp;quot;]is</a> not directed at the blog entry[/URL], as one would hope was evident from his <i>immediately expanding on that statement in terms of &amp;quot;what is the utility of 'the God-Machine is a giant qashmallim'?&amp;quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. Sorry.<br /> <br /> My bad, Mike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T20:08:39-08:00","id":351225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350854#post350854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like how this invites questions about the qashmallim's relationship with the God-Machines angels and the Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bonus round: Consider Demon's &quot;What does it say about the God-Machine that its own limbs can rebel against it?&quot; query in the context of Promethean self-coordination. Then consider the primary theory the Unchained have about qashmallim.<br /> <br /> I like my speculative theology circular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T22:04:05-08:00","id":351338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350668#post350668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Stuff about Dragon Age Inquisition*</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude! Spoiler tags, please?<br /> <br /> (I'm just playin', you're good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T22:19:13-08:00","id":351350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350904#post350904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that each line of the new world of darkness is made with the idea to be it's own universe separated from the other lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... No, they're not. They're generally designed to be <i>played</i> separately, but they're written with the assumption that they all exist in a shared universe. The fact that Mages, Prometheans, and Unchained all understand the universe differently is just human nature... or... supenatural nature, as the case may be. The books just contain a lot of seemingly conflicting information because they're all written as tough the way the eponymous supernatural creatures' understanding of the universe is essentially correct, because if everyone is playing that type of creature, that will probably be what the characters all believe. But they do all exist in a shared universe (unless the ST decides they don't for the purposes of his or her chronicle).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T22:19:45-08:00","id":351351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=350854#post350854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a side note, why do the books always italicize qashmal and qashmllim? Is it because they're words from another language?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per a cursory googling of &quot;italicizing foreign words,&quot; it's likely because it's a foreign word that isn't in Merriam-Webster's and doesn't appear too often in the text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T22:41:23-08:00","id":351362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=351350#post351350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err... No, they're not. They're generally designed to be <i>played</i> separately, but they're written with the assumption that they all exist in a shared universe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well\u2026 they are, except when they\u2019re not. As an example, consider Dave Brookshaw\u2019s comments about the idea of mixing <b>Mage</b> and <b>Hunter</b>: in a nutshell, don\u2019t do it; the games\u2019 fundamental assumptions about the way the world works are incompatible. <b>Mage 2e</b>\u2019s notion of the Sleeping Curse and the utter inability of Sleepers to work around it (culminating in the statement that \u201cif you want hunters in a <b>Mage</b> game, use Banishers\u201d) vs. <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s notion that <i>any</i> supernatural challenge can be overcome with sufficient persistence and ingenuity is the most obvious example where no effort is made to accomodate a \u201cshared universe\u201d model.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-26T23:19:28-08:00","id":351381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=351362#post351362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well\u2026 they are, except when they\u2019re not. As an example, consider Dave Brookshaw\u2019s comments about the idea of mixing <b>Mage</b> and <b>Hunter</b>: in a nutshell, don\u2019t do it; the games\u2019 fundamental assumptions about the way the world works are incompatible. <b>Mage 2e</b>\u2019s notion of the Sleeping Curse and the utter inability of Sleepers to work around it (culminating in the statement that \u201cif you want hunters in a <b>Mage</b> game, use Banishers\u201d) vs. <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s notion that <i>any</i> supernatural challenge can be overcome with sufficient persistence and ingenuity is the most obvious example where no effort is made to accomodate a \u201cshared universe\u201d model.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but I think that's more a product of the games not being designed to be played together. I could be mistaken, but I'm reasonably certain that Task Force Valkyrie, for example, still exists in the World of Darkness, even if you're playing as Mages and TFV isn't really a threat to your characters. Although at that point its a fairly academic distinction, because you're not likely to run into TFV in a mage game specifically because they wouldn't be much of a threat, so the question of whether or not the technically exist if you never see them is a pretty pointless one.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my point is the various game lines are definitely not &quot;made with the idea [for each] to be its own separate universe separated from the other lines.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T01:08:08-08:00","id":351431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=351362#post351362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well\u2026 they are, except when they\u2019re not. As an example, consider Dave Brookshaw\u2019s comments about the idea of mixing <b>Mage</b> and <b>Hunter</b>: in a nutshell, don\u2019t do it; the games\u2019 fundamental assumptions about the way the world works are incompatible. <b>Mage 2e</b>\u2019s notion of the Sleeping Curse and the utter inability of Sleepers to work around it (culminating in the statement that \u201cif you want hunters in a <b>Mage</b> game, use Banishers\u201d) vs. <b>Hunter</b>\u2019s notion that <i>any</i> supernatural challenge can be overcome with sufficient persistence and ingenuity is the most obvious example where no effort is made to accomodate a \u201cshared universe\u201d model.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you can <i>do</i> it, it's just that Hunter for better or worse forgot or chose to ignore the fact that Sleepers forget they witness magic, same as it downplayed the effects of seeing a werewolf. If you run a crossover, you just have to decide which game's right.<br /> <br /> As for the angel - qashmal - angel thing, the blog reproduces about two thirds of the sidebar I wrote on the subject in Promethean 2E. About the only thing extra is pointing out that qashmallim, god-machine angels, and supernal angels can't even <i>see</i> one another unless mmaterialized, as none of them use the same frequency of Twilight!<br /> <br /> The &quot;angels are captured and repurposed qashmallim&quot; thing comes from Demon, by the way. I personally don't see the similarity beyond surface trappings, but if you want it to be true more power to your elbow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T01:56:32-08:00","id":351444,"title":"","content":"Apologies for latching onto this tangent, but I do not believe I ever posted when this was originally going on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=351431#post351431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, you can <i>do</i> it, it's just that Hunter for better or worse forgot or chose to ignore the fact that Sleepers forget they witness magic, same as it downplayed the effects of seeing a werewolf. If you run a crossover, you just have to decide which game's right.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Now, this might be a bit too Hunter: the Reckoning for people, but what if being part of the Vigil was, in fact, a kind of special condition? Including the possibility of a supernatural (possibly even Supernal) sponsor or perhaps just an intrinsic quality of the World of Darkness. Regardless, this condition sets Hunters apart from regular humanity in ways aside from the psychological. This does not make them proper Sleepwalkers, but gives them the ability to force through Quiesence, Lunacy and similar things in ways regular mortals cannot and the ability to risk Willpower.<br /> <br /> This would preserve both games assumptions by making those who have taken up the Vigil into something that is (ever so slightly) apart from the common Sleeping Masses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>:<br /> <br /> Bonus: It would make the &quot;Hunter condition&quot; a Mystery for Mages to explore! Everybody wins (well, except those Mages killed by Hunters, but those surely had it coming)!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","user":"saibot","date":".  Added a thought 12-27-2014, 05:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T02:58:15-08:00","id":351476,"title":"","content":"Even if you do that, Hunter makes assumptions about things like being able to lobotomize magic out of Mages, or use special concussion grenades to break Werewolf shapeshifting, that are totally out of theme with the other lines. It's super science is also out of theme with every other gameline except Demon and that's maybe arguable. Hunter just doesn't play super nice with other lines. It's by no means entirely incompatible, but it takes a lot more work to smooth out the rough edges that're formed when it comes into contact with other lines.<br /> <br /> This is, for many reasons, desirable though. Hunter would be a much worse game if it didn't do this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T04:15:00-08:00","id":351497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eolirin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=351476#post351476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you do that, Hunter makes assumptions about things like being able to lobotomize magic out of Mages, or use special concussion grenades to break Werewolf shapeshifting, that are totally out of theme with the other lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Hunter's defence, though, it also never claims that those things are the protagonists of other gamelines! Perhaps some gutter mages can be lobotomised to remove their magic, perhaps some shapeshifters can be forced out of their lycanthropy with special grenades!<br /> <br /> Regardless, though, I was actually talking more from a Mage perspective. For those STs who would not like their Seers going up against TFV investigating their business or their AKD/GotV Xanatos Pileup to be ruined by &quot;Hunters can't touch this!&quot;.<br /> <br /> That being said, if we want to continue this, it would probably best to reopen the old discussion (wherever it tooks place) or make another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T04:55:16-08:00","id":351509,"title":"","content":"As a general rule I tend to take the information in the books as canon, however if you tell me that this information comes from a wrong interpretation of the protagonists of the line then it makes a lot more sense to me. The problem is, like some people pointed out before, there is a lot of contradictory information between the different lines that makes mixing them very difficult sometimes. Hunter is the worst in terms of mixing, (I love the game by the way). The hunter organizations sometimes give the impression of being ridiculously powerful. It shows that humans are not the helpless victims that the other lines suggest, in fact if you screw humans too much one of the organizations is gonna come to you and they are more than capable of going toe to toe against you if not outright exterminate you, your group and the rest of critters in the city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T05:24:43-08:00","id":351545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things Wood Ingham did in his qashmallim section of Pandora's Book, which I read about twenty times before writing them up for 2E, was point out that there's really no such thing as &quot;Elpidos&quot; or &quot;Lilithim&quot;. Or for that matter Elpis or Flux - it's all just Pyros. The choirs and orders were made up by alchemists and Prometheans to try to classify what they were seeing - no qashmal ever calls itself &quot;a greater Lilithim&quot; or whathaveyou. Or, for that matter, no qashmal ever calls itself a &quot;qashmal&quot; - if you ask one what it is, it'll just say &quot;A Messenger&quot; or &quot;an Agent.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> More of a category than a diagnosis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T05:45:41-08:00","id":351552,"title":"","content":"Indeed; the only reason I brought it up was to demonstrate that yes, sometimes nWoD games <i>do</i> have inconsistencies that are more compatible with the notion of separate universes per gameline than with there being a unified nWoD (any time you have to decide which gameline is \u201cright\u201d, you\u2019re dealing with an inconsistency between them). I\u2019ll freely admit that these inconstancies are the exception rather than the rule; but they <i>do</i> exist \u2014 and sometimes, eliminating them is more trouble than it\u2019s worth. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the \u201cincompatible frequencies of Twilight\u201d clarification, Dave; that\u2019s something else I\u2019ve been curious about for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T06:02:01-08:00","id":351588,"title":"","content":"A 'shared-universe' suggests to me that there's an underlying structure that links the games together. While there is some commonalities such as Twilight, that's generally not the case. The books aren't written to block cross-over but they generally ignore the other settings, and don't allow similarities to limit themselves. Changeling and Mummy both have Fate/ The Wyrd, but the writers seem pretty uninterested in telling us how those two relate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I could be mistaken, but I'm reasonably certain that Task Force Valkyrie, for example, still exists in the World of Darkness, even if you're playing as Mages and TFV isn't really a threat to your characters. </div> </div> </div>That's getting into some weird philosophical areas. You seem to be claiming that there's a platonic world of darkness out there that all the writers are merely describing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T06:59:25-08:00","id":351613,"title":"","content":"The thing is, several lines acknowledged the existence of one another within their own fiction. Im not trying to claim a platonic world of darkness any more than the books themselves present the idea of such a world. Each game is written with the assumption that it will be played indepenently of the other games (with the possible exception of Beast?) and doesn't concern itself with avoiding contradictions with other lines. However, they are also written as though the other lines do exist, they just rarely interact. The contradictions shouldn't really matter outside of crossover games because of everyone's playing a werewolf it doesn't much matter what Mages think of the shadow, and if you are playing Crossover, the ST is going to have to make calls about who's worldview is right and wrong and in what ways no matter what, so the books make a conscious effort not to limit the ST's ability to make those calls by stating &quot;the truth&quot; outright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T08:39:53-08:00","id":351696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=351431#post351431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the angel - qashmal - angel thing, the blog reproduces about two thirds of the sidebar I wrote on the subject in Promethean 2E. About the only thing extra is pointing out that qashmallim, god-machine angels, and supernal angels can't even <i>see</i> one another unless mmaterialized, as none of them use the same frequency of Twilight!</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget <b>Inferno</b>'s empyreans!<br /> <br /> Also, did you happen to write <b>Beast</b>'s ephemeral entities' section, too? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T09:58:33-08:00","id":351772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=351431#post351431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the angel - qashmal - angel thing, the blog reproduces about two thirds of the sidebar I wrote on the subject in Promethean 2E. About the only thing extra is pointing out that qashmallim, god-machine angels, and supernal angels can't even <i>see</i> one another unless mmaterialized, as none of them use the same frequency of Twilight!</div> </div> </div> </div>I was really hoping that qashmal and angel shared the same frequency. Not just for crossover potential, but also that we have too many already.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T10:23:24-08:00","id":351786,"title":"","content":"Honestly putting all the lines into one unified cosmology and metaphysics is a huge endeavor and way too much work. One possible solution to the problem of mixing the different games could be for the writers to include sidebars with suggestions on how to do it. Nothing too elaborated, just general ideas and guides. This way I think we can have both flexibility and clarity without too much constrain or ambiguity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T11:42:32-08:00","id":351878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firanai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=351786#post351786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly putting all the lines into one unified cosmology and metaphysics is a huge endeavor and way too much work. One possible solution to the problem of mixing the different games could be for the writers to include sidebars with suggestions on how to do it. Nothing too elaborated, just general ideas and guides. This way I think we can have both flexibility and clarity without too much constrain or ambiguity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that kind of how it's done now?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T12:07:38-08:00","id":351892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=351878#post351878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't that kind of how it's done now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless I missed something reading the corebooks the way I remember it they don't say much, an stereotype and maybe a little bit of info. Some of the supplements give more material to work but not much more.<br /> The thing is that the creatures of the other lines are described in the most general terms, from things you could have seen in the movies and wikipedia but not from the point of view of the other lines. This is a good approach if you have new players who know nothing of the other lines or if you want to describe things from the point of view of the creature from the line you are reading. However it doesn't give much to the ones who have read them.<br /> However this is just a suggestion since I understand that you cannot put in the book information for every type of player, you have to carefully consider what do you include in it as the space is limited. As far as I'm concerned I'm perfectly happy with just the ideas and suggestions that people give in the forum. The extra material and ideas that they create are very good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 12-27-2014, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T15:17:37-08:00","id":351993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=351772#post351772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was really hoping that qashmal and angel shared the same frequency. Not just for crossover potential, but also that we have too many already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> It's not like qashmallim are interested in what the God-Machine wants all that much, for the same reason Prometheans aren't. Nor is the idea of Twilight frequencies that hard; if they're their own class of ephemeral being, they have a frequency to themselves. If it interacts with other classes, it has a Numina or other advantage that allows it. <br /> <br /> This way, they only interact as much as the story requires them too. And shows that no, they aren't that similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T17:39:47-08:00","id":352128,"title":"","content":"Also, to be fair, putting Angels and Qashmallim into the same Twilight frequency is a super easy mod to make, so if you like it that way better, just do it that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T18:31:54-08:00","id":352154,"title":"","content":"It's more than that - qashmallim aren't actually ephemeral entities at all. They are not made of ephemera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-27T19:37:14-08:00","id":352219,"title":"","content":"I always took \u201cephemeral beings\u201d to be a catch-all term for \u201cbeings that are made of intangible substances\u201d. <b>GMC</b> speaks of ghosts, spirits, and angels not interacting with each other because they\u2019re composed of separate, insubstantial materials (\u201cephemera\u201d); it\u2019s not about \u201cfrequencies\u201d so much as it\u2019s about what interacts with what. <br /> <br /> The Strix are <i>like</i> ephemeral beings without <i>being</i> ephemeral beings because smoke has a lot of traits in common with being ephemeral without actually being ephemeral. Supernal beings (such as seraphim and cherubim) are made of Supernal symbols, which are <i>very much</i> intangible things; but they\u2019re a very different <i>kind</i> of intangible thing than what the God-Machine\u2019s angels are made of. Whether Supernal angels and the God-Machine\u2019s angels should be able to see and interact with each other depends on whether Supernal symbols of Forces and Prime should typically interact with whatever kind of ephemera the God-Machine\u2019s angels are made of (Aether, until I\u2019m told otherwise) \u2014 and as of <b>GMC</b>, the official answer to that is that they don\u2019t. <br /> <br /> And <i>qashmallim</i> are composed of Pyros, which is <i>yet another</i> intangible thing. Once again, the issue is whether Pyros typically interacts with Supernal symbols and/or Aether; and once again, the official answer is \u201cit\u2019s a different kind of intangible; so no.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T06:03:22-08:00","id":352584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=351613#post351613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, they are also written as though the other lines do exist, they just rarely interact.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not clear cut like that. They acknowledge those other creatures exist, but then completely ignore the setting assumptions that would impact them and indeed contradict them at times. The example that springs to mind is the spirits referenced by Cruac. Are they Shadow spirits? At least as far as I remember the answer was, only to the extent that you put the Shadow in your game. The default assumption being that it doesn\u2019t actually exist in Requiem.<br /> <br /> Kinda similiar to how some of the later developers of the CWoD seem to have come to the conclusion that although the settings were all clearly interrelated and referenced each other, they weren't actually the same setting; they were instead kinda narrative parallel universes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T06:51:48-08:00","id":352624,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s worth noting that a stated motivation for the change in the way ephemeral entities (don\u2019t) interact with each other is to facilitate greater isolation of individual gamelines: if spirits and ghosts don\u2019t interact, then [b]Geist[/i] doesn\u2019t have to worry about what the local spirits are up to and <b>Werewolf</b> doesn\u2019t have to worry about what the local ghosts are doing<sup>*</sup>. Frankly, \u201ceach gameline is assumed to exist in its own self-contained world\u201d is the logical conclusion to that line of reasoning: why stop at isolating the intangible entities from each other when you could avoid the cognitive dissonance of why the local vampires, werewolves, and mages don\u2019t interact with each other by saying that, by default, they don\u2019t live in the same universe? i<br /> <br /> <hr />* Unless, of course, you\u2019re dealing with a Werewolf pack that actively seeks out ghosts or a Sin-Eater krewe that is heavily invested in spirits; but in such cases, you\u2019re <i>opting in</i> to a larger-than-normal canvas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T12:04:09-08:00","id":352948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=352624#post352624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s worth noting that a stated motivation for the change in the way ephemeral entities (don\u2019t) interact with each other is to facilitate greater isolation of individual gamelines: if spirits and ghosts don\u2019t interact, then [b]Geist[/i] doesn\u2019t have to worry about what the local spirits are up to and <b>Werewolf</b> doesn\u2019t have to worry about what the local ghosts are doing<sup>*</sup>. Frankly, \u201ceach gameline is assumed to exist in its own self-contained world\u201d is the logical conclusion to that line of reasoning: why stop at isolating the intangible entities from each other when you could avoid the cognitive dissonance of why the local vampires, werewolves, and mages don\u2019t interact with each other by saying that, by default, they don\u2019t live in the same universe? i<br /> <hr />* Unless, of course, you\u2019re dealing with a Werewolf pack that actively seeks out ghosts or a Sin-Eater krewe that is heavily invested in spirits; but in such cases, you\u2019re <i>opting in</i> to a larger-than-normal canvas.</div> </div> </div> </div>You answered your own question with your asterisk. The WoD that exists around each table is a separate unique, and utterly individual universe; the point of the rules is to provide the maximal amount of tools for generating whatever each group wants with as little difficulty as possible. That requires both working under the assumption that the lines exist together, and also taking steps to minimize the surface area of those assumptions to as minimal a space as necessary. It's why Supernatural Tolerance exists even as the various twilight beings don't interact with each other.<br /> <br /> Of course, in some cases, like Hunter, the core premise of the setting requires ignoring aspects of the other settings. And thematic importance trumps crossover. But it's very difficult to start with a default of &quot;you're the only supernatural type&quot; while still providing the necessary tools to enable crossover. It's a lot easier to start with &quot;you all exist together but only interact as much as the ST wants you to&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":614,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","user":"Eolirin","date":". 12-28-2014, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/614-eolirin","name":"Eolirin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T12:05:19-08:00","id":352949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=352624#post352624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s worth noting that a stated motivation for the change in the way ephemeral entities (don\u2019t) interact with each other is to facilitate greater isolation of individual gamelines: if spirits and ghosts don\u2019t interact, then [b]Geist[/i] doesn\u2019t have to worry about what the local spirits are up to and <b>Werewolf</b> doesn\u2019t have to worry about what the local ghosts are doing<sup>*</sup>.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a useful addition in the case of Werewolf and Geist, because given the nature of Hisil spirits, they'd be constantly trying to mug the Geist mythos for Essence (actually a major reason why I favour giving ghosts - and angels - a different form of fuel).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Frankly, \u201ceach gameline is assumed to exist in its own self-contained world\u201d is the logical conclusion to that line of reasoning: why stop at isolating the intangible entities from each other when you could avoid the cognitive dissonance of why the local vampires, werewolves, and mages don\u2019t interact with each other by saying that, by default, they don\u2019t live in the same universe? </div> </div> </div>There are more spirits than werewolves and mages put together, more ghosts than sineaters, and more angels than demons. The formers are the where the lines would inevitably interact; the latter are easier to keep separate.<br /> <br /> Personally, though, I would turn the implication round and think about how they'd interact.<br /> <br /> <br /> Those Qashmalim are pretty cool, huh?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T13:29:49-08:00","id":353053,"title":"","content":"The different creatures existing in the same universe is not really a problem for one simple reason, each creature from each line has a a very different objective compared to the others. Vampires want blood and territory, werewolves keep an eye on spirits, mages develop their magic and fight the seers, changelings hide form the true fae, prometheans are on a pilgrimage etc....as a general rule they have little reason to interact with each other. Also what do they have to gain from interacting with each other? Too many uncertainties and unknowns, taking into account how dangerous and paranoid the world of darkness is interacting is just more trouble than its worth it. In our games we assume that as a general rule they ignore each other, basically a &quot;live and let live&quot; attitude. They only talk when there is no other way and then forget about each other as fast as possible.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Qashmalim I have to say that I love them and the idea behind them. In fact I would very much like to see a line or a supplement devoted to them and their mysterious origin and master: The principle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T13:33:16-08:00","id":353056,"title":"","content":"Wait, are not default assumption to be &quot;every monster <i>race</i> live in World of Darkness, just they do not generally interact with each other&quot;?<br /> <br /> As to other thing - literally today I start to make some preparation for my <b>Promethean</b>-<b>Demon</b>-<b>Mage</b> game and I started to think about implications of whole &quot;angelology&quot; of nWoD, as it will be major point of planned game. So default assumption of gameline is that Qashmalim, God Machine Angels and Supernal Aether Angels are all different beings and do not interact with each other, correct? If yes, what would rules need to accumulate the same, or at least similar origin of them? Like that Qashmalims were so posed to use the God Machine Angels as their Earth vessels? Or that Qashmalims are &quot;rouge&quot; and somehow &quot;lower/fallen&quot; Supernal Angels? What would be crossover issues with this kind of thought?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-28T15:56:51-08:00","id":353208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/349040-the-scintillating-flame-\u2013-qashmallim-open-dev?p=353056#post353056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, are not default assumption to be &quot;every monster <i>race</i> live in World of Darkness, just they do not generally interact with each other&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. Even the more populous supernaturals aren't common enough that every city has a support structure in place (see especially SEs and Prometheans), and that's before the fact that &quot;if it doesn't have anything to do with you, ignore it and hope it stays that way&quot; as a heuristic for encountering unknown supernatural phenomena isn't limited to mortals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}